1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,720
The admin menu lists the pages of the admin, but your team uses

2
00:00:04,720 --> 00:00:06,607
only a few of them every day.

3
00:00:06,607 --> 00:00:11,028
The Admin Menu module lets you add your own links, grouped the way you work.

4
00:00:11,028 --> 00:00:13,670
Let's build a menu, and decide who sees it.

5
00:00:18,270 --> 00:00:22,065
An admin menu is a named set of items, and each item is

6
00:00:22,065 --> 00:00:25,051
an admin node, which can hold other nodes.

7
00:00:25,051 --> 00:00:29,032
Orchard Core adds the enabled menus to its own admin menu.

8
00:00:29,032 --> 00:00:33,200
They change the admin only, never the site your visitors see.

9
00:00:33,950 --> 00:00:36,254
Four kinds of node are available:

10
00:00:36,254 --> 00:00:40,034
a link opens a page, and a placeholder groups other nodes.

11
00:00:40,034 --> 00:00:44,464
Content Types adds a link for each content type you choose, and Lists

12
00:00:44,464 --> 00:00:48,540
adds a link for each item that holds a list, such as each blog.

13
00:00:52,795 --> 00:00:55,961
Admin menus live under Tools, Admin Menus.

14
00:00:55,961 --> 00:00:59,523
The Blog recipe turns the Admin Menu feature on.

15
00:00:59,523 --> 00:01:04,865
On a site where it is off, enable the feature first, under Tools, Features.

16
00:01:05,330 --> 00:01:09,162
The Blog recipe also creates a menu named Admin menus.

17
00:01:09,162 --> 00:01:14,720
Each row shows whether a menu is enabled, and offers Edit Nodes, Edit and Delete.

18
00:01:14,720 --> 00:01:18,170
The Actions button disables or enables the menu.

19
00:01:18,652 --> 00:01:21,147
Edit Nodes shows the tree of a menu.

20
00:01:21,147 --> 00:01:26,254
Blog and Main Menu are links, and Content is a placeholder with nodes inside it.

21
00:01:26,254 --> 00:01:29,402
The admin menu on the left shows these entries.

22
00:01:33,643 --> 00:01:36,868
On the list, Add Admin Menu asks for a name only.

23
00:01:36,868 --> 00:01:40,503
Let's call the menu Editor Shortcuts, and select Create.

24
00:01:40,958 --> 00:01:43,948
The menu is listed as Enabled, with no nodes.

25
00:01:43,948 --> 00:01:47,819
A menu appears in the admin menu only when it is enabled and

26
00:01:47,819 --> 00:01:49,578
holds at least one node.

27
00:01:53,820 --> 00:01:56,734
Edit Nodes opens the tree, which is empty.

28
00:01:56,734 --> 00:01:59,831
Add Node lists the kinds of node you can add.

29
00:01:59,831 --> 00:02:03,474
The Link Admin Node adds a link with a text and a Url,

30
00:02:03,474 --> 00:02:04,810
so let's add it.

31
00:02:05,365 --> 00:02:10,064
Link Text is the label in the admin menu, and Link Url is where it goes.

32
00:02:10,064 --> 00:02:14,342
An address without a leading slash is relative to the root of the

33
00:02:14,342 --> 00:02:17,415
admin site, so Media opens the media library.

34
00:02:17,896 --> 00:02:22,551
Target decides where the link opens, for example in a separate tab.

35
00:02:22,551 --> 00:02:27,206
A full web address, such as one for another site, is used as it is.

36
00:02:27,746 --> 00:02:29,763
Pick opens the list of icons.

37
00:02:29,763 --> 00:02:32,759
Type a word to search it, then select an icon.

38
00:02:32,759 --> 00:02:36,216
The icon shows beside the link text in the admin menu.

39
00:02:36,692 --> 00:02:41,062
Create adds the node to the tree, and Media Library appears in the

40
00:02:41,062 --> 00:02:42,822
admin menu on the left.

41
00:02:42,822 --> 00:02:45,552
Select it, and the media library opens.

42
00:02:49,814 --> 00:02:53,394
Add Node also offers the Placeholder Admin Node:

43
00:02:53,394 --> 00:02:56,112
a menu item that holds other nodes.

44
00:02:56,112 --> 00:03:01,284
It has no address of its own, only a Link Text, an icon and permissions.

45
00:03:01,737 --> 00:03:05,507
Let's name it Editorial, pick an icon, and select Create.

46
00:03:05,507 --> 00:03:09,277
The placeholder is added to the tree after Media Library.

47
00:03:14,091 --> 00:03:16,029
Nesting is done by dragging.

48
00:03:16,029 --> 00:03:19,505
Drag Media Library onto Editorial, and it moves inside.

49
00:03:19,505 --> 00:03:21,841
The tree shows it below its parent.

50
00:03:22,358 --> 00:03:26,682
In the admin menu, Editorial is a group with Media Library inside.

51
00:03:26,682 --> 00:03:31,668
A placeholder shows only when it holds at least one item that has an address.

52
00:03:35,918 --> 00:03:40,098
Content Types adds a link for each content type you select.

53
00:03:40,098 --> 00:03:45,371
Tick Blog Post and Page, or choose Show All Content Types to add every type.

54
00:03:45,371 --> 00:03:46,978
Then select Create.

55
00:03:47,497 --> 00:03:51,657
Lists adds a link for each content item of a type that holds a list.

56
00:03:51,657 --> 00:03:55,872
Choose the Blog content type, and clear Add parent menu item, so that

57
00:03:55,872 --> 00:03:59,582
the links to the blogs are not grouped under a parent entry.

58
00:03:59,582 --> 00:04:00,987
Then select Create.

59
00:04:01,463 --> 00:04:04,789
Drag both nodes onto Editorial, as before.

60
00:04:04,789 --> 00:04:09,432
Its group lists Media Library, Blog Post, Page and each blog.

61
00:04:09,432 --> 00:04:14,283
A blog added later gets its link without any change to the menu.

62
00:04:18,505 --> 00:04:20,687
A node can require permissions.

63
00:04:20,687 --> 00:04:25,820
In the Permissions field of Media Library, choose Manage Media, then select Save.

64
00:04:25,820 --> 00:04:29,065
Only users who have that permission see the item.

65
00:04:29,524 --> 00:04:34,864
Each menu also has its own permission, named View Admin Menu followed by the menu name.

66
00:04:34,864 --> 00:04:38,539
Search for it on a role's edit page and allow it, and that

67
00:04:38,539 --> 00:04:41,583
role sees the menu items its permissions allow.

68
00:04:41,583 --> 00:04:44,454
The Administrator role has every permission.

69
00:04:44,911 --> 00:04:49,134
To hide a whole menu, open Actions on the list and choose Disable.

70
00:04:49,134 --> 00:04:52,711
Its nodes leave the admin menu until you choose Enable.

71
00:04:52,711 --> 00:04:56,171
A node has the same choice, beside its Delete button.

72
00:05:00,371 --> 00:05:05,471
To use your menus on another site, add the Admin Menus step to a deployment plan.

73
00:05:05,471 --> 00:05:07,464
It exports every admin menu.

74
00:05:07,464 --> 00:05:11,099
A recipe can also create menus when a site is set up, as

75
00:05:11,099 --> 00:05:12,681
the Blog recipe does.

76
00:05:14,681 --> 00:05:18,778
Admin menus put the pages your team uses in one place, grouped your

77
00:05:18,778 --> 00:05:21,022
way, and shown to the right roles.

78
00:05:21,022 --> 00:05:22,481
Thanks for watching.

